# Implement source and claim provenance

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation notes concern structural admission. The bounded
design below is not a running model or verified educational output.

Distinguish provided, derived, cited, and unverified content and link every
citation to the exact claim and source metadata the user must review. Keep that
semantic provenance separate from application transaction provenance recording
whether an accepted mutation entered through direct human editing,
clipboard-assisted model response, CLI, or MCP.

The provenance-only acceptance case is now executable for one existing
revision-owned provenance record: kind and optional source reference can change
while claim text, claim identity, claim-to-record linkage, and unrelated source
records remain stable. Claim-level assignment and removal are also executable
for existing block and inline-span targets through admitted provenance
identities; they preserve authored content and remain atomic with other generic
families on the same target. Undo restores the prior linkage.

A transport-neutral citation-review linkage now additionally requires every
cited claim in a review set to resolve through its exact assigned revision-owned
`Provenance` record and from there to at least one exact source-metadata
identity.
The validator derives `Cited` status from that record rather than a copied claim
field. Links to unknown
claims,
unknown sources, unknown or duplicated provenance records, mismatched
provenance links, non-cited claims, duplicate claims/sources, or duplicate exact
claim/source relationships reject with typed
structural errors. Multiple distinct sources for one cited claim remain valid.

After full structural validation, read-only projections return one claim's exact
assigned revision-owned provenance record plus its linked source identities or
exact reviewable source records in caller link order. A constructor-sealed
validated review now retains that exact admitted set so repeated claim
projections do not rescan structural linkage. The provenance projection borrows
the authoritative semantic record without copying its kind or source reference,
while source-record projection preserves caller-owned metadata without parsing,
ranking, normalization, or quality judgment. Valid non-cited claims project no
sources, and unknown requested claims remain typed failures.

A 32-case compact oracle crosses all four semantic provenance kinds with link
presence, source presence, and provenance-identity match state to pin the same
failure precedence through direct and sealed admission. All ten structural
error classes also require exact direct/sealed rejection parity, so none can
produce constructor-sealed review evidence. Source retrieval, source-quality
policy, citation
parsing/formatting, and review UI remain separate.

The task remains open for source retrieval/admission, a concrete source-metadata
schema, source-quality and claim-sufficiency policy, provenance diagnostics,
citation parsing/formatting and review UI, candidate-response integration, and
cross-adapter projection. Those owners must consume the existing revision-owned
provenance and citation linkage rather than inventing parallel source status.

## Finite semantic claim, source and transaction provenance contract

**Inputs:** stable source identities, exact quoted or cited source spans,
accepted semantic claim IDs, claim-kind declarations and an independently
trusted application mutation origin. **Outputs:** a source-to-claim graph
retaining provided, derived, cited or unverified status, plus visible
citation/export annotations, or one typed missing/ambiguous-source refusal.
Semantic content provenance is independent from *who initiated* an edit.

**Four semantic classes:** `Provided` means source text directly supplied by
the user; `Derived` is explicitly reasoned from exact referenced claims;
`Cited` has a verifiable source metadata link and a user-review state;
`Unverified` carries an unresolved claim with no accepted support. A source
record retains identity, title/author if known, acquisition mode, content
fingerprint, quoted range and review status. Unknown author or timestamp is
recorded as absent, not fabricated. Citation format is a presentation choice,
not a proof that external content was verified.

**Worked three-claim ledger:** source `src-1`, supplied text `The sample is
10 mm long`, has a stable exact offset/owner. Claim `c1` repeats 10 mm and
is `Provided(src-1)`; `c2` computes doubled length 20 mm and is
`Derived(c1)` with arithmetic justification.

Claim `c3`, `The sample was
collected in Madrid`, is `Unverified` because the location is absent.
The export annotation for `c1` names `src-1`; `c2` names `c1` and identifies
its derivation; `c3` prints `Source not established` and must not silently
acquire a citation. A notebook edit preserves those claim IDs/references
unless a backend-accepted change explicitly invalidates them.

**Separate mutation provenance:** a trusted human edit, clipboard-reviewed
model candidate, CLI Apply or MCP Apply is stamped at the application adapter
after authorization and linked to the accepted transaction receipt. Source
content cannot self-assign this stamp. A model-derived sentence may enter
through a human-edited transaction without becoming `Provided`, and a
CLI-authored citation remains `Cited` only when source evidence warrants it.

**Refusal example:** a citation targets a missing `src-9`, a claim
misrepresents an unsupported quoted range, two source IDs conflict, or an
unreviewed web page is presented as verified. Retain a visible `Unverified`
or blocking citation diagnostic; no auto-retrieval or forged bibliography.
If an Export lacks a supported citation projection, omit the false link and
mark the claim unresolved rather than claiming complete provenance.

**Assumptions and limits:** typed source/claim owner links and revision-bound
structural admission exist. Full source metadata, retrieval, citation
formatting, quality judgment, review UI and cross-adapter audit projection
are incomplete. The three claims are a finite provenance policy, not
verification of any external citation or all application event origins.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for graph and revision linkage; theoretical for
  source metadata, review and Export annotations, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** supplied source and three claims, four status rules,
  distinct trusted transaction origin and unresolved/missing-source refusals.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** source retrieval, substantive
  fact-checking, citation UI, complete audit transport or rendered footnotes.
